        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"cnranger\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/53a042/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> cnranger:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If its anything like comics they probably lose in the first few meetings with the villain before rallying and winning in the end. What would you consider a hero loss?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Like, the heroes fail at stopping an event, and a new team comes in, or heroes die. Knowing lots about comics, the heroes also tend to win \"in the end\".</p>\n<p>I was just curious if those battles were docemented. If not, then no need to add them! I don't want to derail this thread from XtremeGuardian's awesome project.&nbsp; I wouldn't mind having another thread about \"losses\" unless it came help out the document.</p>\n<p>Sorry to cut it short.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
